/**
 * The raw layer of Windows: the natives of `runtime/os/windows.c`, which exist in a Windows build only. The manifest
 * says so (`availableOn`), and a call that the build for another system reaches is a compile error there - reach it
 * from a `.Windows` arm of `match OperatingSystem.current`.
 *
 * It is not the documented surface of `std/os`: the OS-neutral modules call it from their Windows arm.
 */

/** The natives only Windows has, one per call of the Windows API. */
public native type Windows {
  /**
   * Milliseconds since the system started (`GetTickCount64`).
   *
   * # Examples
   *
   *     print Windows.tickCount()
   */
  native static fn tickCount(): Int64
}
